-- title:
--   Integrating out the centre over a determinant slab
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a number field, write $G = \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_F)$ for `AdelicGL2`, let $H$ be `rationalTorusUnipotent F`, the subgroup of $G$ generated by the rational central and rational $\mathrm{diag}(a,1)$ points together with the adelic unipotent subgroup, let $\nu$ be the quotient measure `rationalTorusUnipotentQuotientMeasure F` on the orbit quotient $H\backslash G$ (the pushforward along $g \mapsto Hg$ of adelic Haar measure with the density attached to the chosen Haar measure on $H$), let $\mathbf{K} =$ `adelicMaximalCompact F` be the subgroup of $g$ whose finite component lies in the full level-zero integral subgroup and whose component at each infinite place has determinant of absolute value $1$ and preserves the row-wise quadratic form, equipped with the Haar measure of total mass one, let $d^\times$ denote idelic Haar measure and $\|t\| =$ `ideleNorm F t` the module character of $t$ on $\mathbb{A}_F$. Assume given: a constant $c \neq \infty$ in $[0,\infty]$ such that for all measurable fundamental domains $D, D'$ for the group of principal idèles (the image of $F^\times$) acting on the idèles, and every measurable $f \colon G \to [0,\infty]$ with $f(xg) = f(g)$ for all $x \in H$, the lower integral of $f$ on representatives over $H\backslash G$ against $\nu$ equals $c \int_{D}\int_{D'}\int_{\mathbf{K}} f(z\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k)\,\|t\|^{-1}\,dk\,d^\times t\,d^\times z$; a measurable fundamental domain $D$ for the principal idèles; a constant $V \notin \{0,\infty\}$ such that $\int_D f(\|z\|)\,d^\times z = V\int_0^\infty f(y)\,y^{-1}\,dy$ for all measurable $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to [0,\infty]$; reals $0 < d_1 \le d_2$; measurable $\Phi_1, \Phi_2 \colon G \to \mathbb{C}$, each left invariant under $H$, such that $\Phi_1\overline{\Phi_2}$ is unchanged when $z\,\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k$ is replaced by $\mathrm{diag}(t,1)\,k$, and such that $(t,k) \mapsto \Phi_1(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\overline{\Phi_2(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)}$ is integrable for the product of $\|t\|^{-1}\,d^\times t$ restricted to $D$ with the Haar measure of $\mathbf{K}$. Then $q \mapsto \Phi_1\overline{\Phi_2}$ evaluated at a representative of $q$ is integrable for $\nu$ over the slab $\{q : \|\det q\| \in [d_1,d_2]\}$, and its integral there equals $c\,V\,\tfrac{1}{2}\log(d_2/d_1)$ (the real scalars $c$ and $V$ taken as real numbers, the product viewed in $\mathbb{C}$) times $\int_D \|t\|^{-1}\int_{\mathbf{K}} \Phi_1(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)\overline{\Phi_2(\mathrm{diag}(t,1)k)}\,dk\,d^\times t$.
--
--   This is the Iwasawa-coordinate disintegration of an inner product over the torus–unipotent quotient, restricted to a window $d_1 \le \|\det\| \le d_2$: the central variable contributes only the factor $V\log(d_2/d_1)/2$, leaving a pairing over the idèle fundamental domain and the maximal compact subgroup. It is used in the analytic continuation of inner products of pseudo-Eisenstein series against their Weyl intertwining terms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AutomorphicForm_integrableOn_and_setIntegral_rationalTorusUnipotentQuotient_slab_mul_conj_eq_mul_setIntegral_inv_ideleNorm_smul_integral_maximalCompact.lean

